==Latin==

===Etymology===
Literally, "with thumb turned".

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|pollice versō}}

===Phrase===
{{head|la|phrase|head=[[pollex|pollice]] [[versus|versō]]|g=m}}

# with the [[thumb]] [[turn]]ed (how spectators indicated favor or displeasure at gladiatorial games).

====Usage notes====
Despite depictions common in movies, it is not clear whether the [[thumbs up]] or [[thumbs down]] indicated displeasure.

